<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $23.99 bln on Feb 7.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $23.99 bln on Feb 7.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $23.99 billion on February 7, 1997 from $23.97 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Feb 7	 Jan 31	 Feb 9</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     19,868	19,848	 15,891</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,097	 4,097	  4,587</p>
<p>    SDRs				    28	    28	     54</p>
<p>    Total			     23,993	23,973	 20,532</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
